The known carrier vector is exactly unchanged from Z1: DEP 1360 mg; TEC 720 mg; DPG 326.6666667 mg; IPM 23.3333333 mg; ethanol 70 mg. Free DEP is counted once: it is included within 1360 mg, not an additional amount on top.

### Stock truth

The specified Orivone 10% w/w DEP, Heliotropal 10% w/w DEP and Coumarin 20% w/w DEP working stocks remain **NOT PREPARED**. Their existing Z1 preparation specifications are carried forward without changing strength: 100 mg Orivone + 900 mg DEP; 100 mg Heliotropal/piperonal + 900 mg DEP; 1000 mg Coumarin powder + 4000 mg DEP. These are future final-build specifications, not requests for separate perfume test samples. A stated mass recipe does not establish dissolution, homogeneity or stability. Do not relabel an existing unspecified-basis stock. No intermediate smell tests are required.

Alpha Irone is the owned 10% w/w DEP stock. Ambrox Super is 25% w/w, from 3 g product + 7 g DPG + 0.5 g IPM + 1.5 g ethanol. Tonkarome is 20% w/w in TEC from 4 g product + 16 g TEC. AIMI is one physical product, not two bottles inferred from duplicated names. Current inventory and authority pins were checked without editing them.

### Nominal 30 mL bottle and concentration

The earlier nominal target remains a measured 6.00 mL aliquot of homogeneous raw-stock concentrate, then permitted ethanol q.s. to a measured 30.00 mL final volume. This is 20% v/v raw-stock concentrate, not 20% w/w and not 20% pure odorants. A 6.500 g master is not assumed to occupy 6.500 or 6.000 mL; do not assume it supplies a particular aliquot without measurement. Actual finished ppm and physical individual volumes remain unknown. Scale all master masses uniformly if necessary; do not alter individual ratios to reach a volume.

For an eventual weighed aliquot: finished product ppm_i = concentrate product ppm_i × aliquot mass / final bottle mass. The owned 96% ethanol's concentration basis remains unspecified.

## Computational evidence and limits

See [selection report](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/a48f/perfume-chem/docs/research/Prada_LHomme_Intense_Zero_Astra_Z2_Selection_Report_20260905.md) and [canonical accounting](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/a48f/perfume-chem/docs/research/Prada_LHomme_Intense_Zero_Astra_Z2_accounting.json). The search covers 289 distinct compositions across the grid, targeted alternatives and local refinements. Recorded duplicates are disclosed in the report.

For the final declared stock-mass scenario, the source-informed 25 C model raises AIMI/Iso E and AIMI/Hedione OAV screening ratios by 29.18% and 30.16%, and lowers Heliotropal/AIMI by 64.15%. These are **not** perceived contribution, similarity, liking or performance improvements. Shared-factor sensitivity checks are algebraic and not independent evidence. Asymmetric candidate-specific gamma residuals can reverse the iris/space ratio preference; no robust perceptual optimum is claimed.

Sandalore, Romandolide, Dihydro Beta Ionone and Hexyl Salicylate still have low seed-model OAVs. The first three have intended odor functions; their low modeled values remain functional alarms, not proof of uselessness and not instructions to increase doses blindly. Hexyl Salicylate's blending role also remains a hypothesis. Tonkarome's finite legacy OAV is an unvalidated proprietary-product proxy. Cedar and patchouli use partial literature composite profiles, not owned-lot analyses.

