## Parent interpretation and acceptance boundary

The integrated release diagnostic remains **FAIL**, not a physical release. Its report header omits the separate chassis-integrity SKIP; the full JSON is authoritative for gate counts. The final selection remains computational only.

The immediate-parent active-dose and OAV-per-time guard **passed**, with both parent and temporal comparisons available and no findings. Artifact arithmetic, report consistency and source-preservation checks passed; the [final verification receipt](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/a48f/perfume-chem/output/prada_lhomme_intense_zero_astra_z2/verification_receipt.json) binds the selected files and numerical outputs. The existing focused software tests also passed (62 tests). None of these results overrides the physical-release hold.

The five failing gates are the preflight aggregate, stock contract, unknown Intense reference, unknown Intense archetype and combined-confidence floor. The stock issues include one AIMI identity represented by duplicate runtime records, the three proposed working-stock preparations and Tonkarome's stale runtime basis/carrier binding. Current source inventories support the declared mass design, but no registry pin was hand-edited to force these gates. The missing base-Prada neroli/geranium/pepper markers do not redefine the Intense target.

The legacy formatter's receptor dose caps, cedar sedation assertion, Tonkarome glycoside-release claim, 99% musk coverage, zero-natural-complexity verdict and assumed retail-margin calculation are **not accepted evidence** for this composition. Natural composite data are partial and not owned-batch measurements. OAV-family and note percentages are not sensory contribution. The 14/100 diagnostic is not a probability of success. Rounded zero vapor or OAV values in narrative subsections must not replace the unrounded JSON.

Source-informed alternatives correct only isolated scenario inputs and are recorded separately in the selection report. They do not silently alter the raw report or grant it sensory, safety or physical authority. Relevant physical readiness and complete safety review still precede any eventual complete-blend use; no intermediate physical comparison is required for this computational selection.
